## Shared compatible metadata adapter (TL329, 2026-10-29)

- Replaced the personal APInex collector with one current metadata adapter for
  the real stored node types `openai-compatible` and `anthropic-compatible`.
  It uses the native decrypted connection getter, protocol auth roles, outbound
  guards/proxy resolution, shared model normalization, and current per-source
  persistence. The old hook and namespace are removed without a compatibility
  reader.
- One URL builder serves validation and discovery for existing relative paths
  and same-origin absolute `modelsPath` values; provider-node create/update
  schemas and validation use the same builder. Configured endpoint failure does
  not probe another URL. Anthropic pagination must complete before a snapshot
  replacement. Snapshots retain exact raw IDs, sanitized source URL, timestamp,
  normalized name/limits/selected capabilities, and explicit finite
  non-negative per-million prices only.
- Integrated review findings were resolved: duplicate raw IDs are omitted so
  prior metadata/prices cannot survive an ambiguous complete response, and the
  design no longer claims catalog and source-snapshot writes are atomic. Source
  audit also extended the existing create/update schemas and validation route
  to accept same-origin absolute endpoints through the shared builder. A stale
  duplicate APInex freshness SHALL was removed from the superseded spec.
- Pricing and strict-zero evidence require fresh, unanimous exact prices across
  currently active connections that expose the raw ID. Unknown, conflicting,
  stale, future, duplicate-ID, and excluded-connection data fail closed.
  Current explicit false capability evidence takes precedence over canonical
  defaults while existing operator/provider overrides retain priority.
- Primary Anthropic docs verification found `image_input.supported` and
  `server_tools` in the documented nested shape, with no `tool_use` field.
  Removed the unsupported `tool_use` inference; `server_tools` remains unknown
  for caller tool-call support. See the package's
  [`completion.review`](openspec/changes/archive/2026-10-30-generic-compatible-model-metadata/completion.review)
  for detailed evidence and fixture sources.
- Focused compatible metadata/discovery/capability/endpoint-schema/models.dev/
  benchmark suite: **89/89 passed**. The existing models.dev live-API test
  performs a public catalog GET; compatible provider fetches are mocked.
  Focused changed-module lint, `git diff --check`, and strict validation for the
  new and superseded packages pass. Prettier passes on changed code and OpenSpec
  except `src/app/api/provider-nodes/[id]/route.ts`, whose clean-base source also
  fails formatting; unrelated existing formatting remains untouched. Full
  changed-file lint reports 11 pre-existing errors in unchanged route/test
  lines. Core typecheck remains nonzero with 720 diagnostics exactly matching
  clean base; no changed production module has a diagnostic.
- Code Simplifier was applied after implementation fixes. Fresh integrated
  independent review returned no actionable findings; the reviewer ran no
