## APInex native node type selection correction (2026-10-29)

- Deployed read-only inspection found the configured APInex node uses stored
  type `openai-compatible`, endpoint `https://api.apinex.bond/v1`, and 44
  synced raw model IDs. The adapter selected only `openai-compatible-chat`,
  which prevented any APInex fetch. The official public catalog returned 44
  structured rows with 21 numeric zero/zero records.
- The native creation schema stores `type = "openai-compatible"`; `apiType =
  "chat"` is a separate request-format field. The route builds IDs with
  `openai-compatible-<apiType>-...`, so `openai-compatible-chat-` is an ID
  prefix, not a stored type. The parent explained this distinction to the
  owner, who accepted the correction. `anthropic-compatible` remains a separate
  family without an established APInex endpoint contract.
- Corrected the selector and predicate to require stored type
  `openai-compatible` and the existing endpoint. All schema-valid API formats
  remain eligible only for raw IDs already synced under their full node ID.
  The strict filter and candidate, visibility, freshness, pricing, and routing
  paths remain unchanged.
- TDD reproduced the deployed failure with the exact native node and 44 exact
  source model IDs. The extended regression validates that live chat shape
  and all other schema-valid API formats while keeping stored type
  `openai-compatible`; it verifies 21 zero and 23 paid rows, exact full-ID/raw-
  ID binding, public-prefix rejection, unrelated Anthropic/endpoint rejection,
  and unchanged synced records/hidden state. Focused verification passes
  **34/34**, including the benchmark hook and existing capabilities and pricing
  suites. Changed-module TypeScript diagnostics pass.
- Strict OpenSpec validation and `git diff --check` pass. Prettier passes for
  changed TypeScript and OpenSpec Markdown files. The root `completion.review`
  check reports one unchanged wrapping difference also present at base
  `e5be44c4080f228bc022ac9f821e073faddf80a8`. Code Simplifier was applied.
  Fresh independent review first found stale dual-type wording after the
  source clarification; it was corrected, and the reviewer confirmed no
