## Normalizer evidence-quote contract follow-up (2026-10-27)

- The normalizer prompt now requires `evidence_quote` to be an exact,
  contiguous, verbatim excerpt from one returned result title or snippet. The
  parser now enforces the same rule instead of concatenating the two fields;
  it continues to validate model identity, benchmark fields, URL membership,
  dates, and values.
- TDD reproduced the parser accepting a quote spanning title and snippet;
  regression now rejects that quote and a paraphrase. The normalizer-request
  prompt regression also checks the exact-quote instruction.
- Code Simplifier review kept the change to one prompt instruction and one
  per-field substring check. Independent Luna-high review confirmed prompt and
  parser alignment, with no routing or cooldown change and no remaining finding.
- Verification: `modelBenchmarkSearch.test.ts` 41/41, focused prompt/parser
  regressions 2/2 after formatting, Prettier checks all changed TypeScript and
  OpenSpec files, and `git diff --check` passes.
- The prior live invalid response body was not retained, so its causal link to
  this prompt/parser mismatch remains unproven. At 06:27:04 UTC the already-due
  production queue retry began its normal source search and, at 06:27:05 UTC,
  logged a POST through `auto/general_high_so:free`. The normal route timed out
  after 600 seconds at 06:37:05 UTC: target 1 (`nvidia/z-ai/glm-5.3-flash`)
  timed out and Auto tried the next target; target 2 (`dots-studio/dots-3-note-preview:free`
  on OpenRouter) returned HTTP 200 but was rejected because
  `finish_reason=length` left no content; Auto then tried further in-band
  targets. No HTTP 429 occurred. A read-only DB check found the row
  `review_required`, queue attempts=3, and `retry_after_at=06:52:05.799Z`;
  queue attempts are not provider-call counts. No normalizer output was
  accepted. No request was manually triggered; Auto, provider settings,
  candidate pool, cooldowns, and queue state were not changed. Follow-up commit
  `78b751a266ed039c1f1cca4361a3c336ad874ac6` is pushed on
  `fix/benchmark-normalizer-verbatim-evidence-20261027` in open PR #38; it is not
  merged or deployed. Live acceptance remains open.

