## Free auto-band quality-source review closeout — 2026-10-25

- Re-read the official Artificial Analysis API schema and examples. The Free
  list exposes configuration-specific rows by `id` and `name`; its example is
  `gpt-oss-20B (high)` with Coding and Intelligence indices. The schema does
  not define a normalized effort field. Pro adds `reasoning_model: boolean`,
  while reasoning token/cost fields describe usage. The parser now trusts a
  recognized API-name suffix before paired chart metadata.
- Candidate scores use the effective mode recorded by Hermes for that band.
  A mapped `xhigh` row is used even when a `high` sibling exists; if that
  mapped row is missing, the sibling remains numeric but is marked as an
  estimate. Generic high reference populations prefer `high`, then `xhigh`.
  Missing-effort values are never converted to zero.
- Independent review findings were corrected: unreviewed punctuation-similar
  model names remain distinct unless an exact reviewed alias maps them; equal
  scores from different agents remain separate observations; singleton
  evidence text matches the five-identity cohort minimum; candidate effort
  matching and sibling fallback provenance agree across code, tests, and spec.
- Recalculation yields 78 provider/model rows, 66 raw model IDs, numeric
  evidence for 43 IDs, 23 without numeric evidence, and no provider-copy
  conflicts. The generated table SHA-256 is
  `3e753f3c3f6bfd35ecaa995a69d6f512c1b8f975f311708da8ca98f8e4bcecd9`.
  Configured band ranges, including the 0.70 high cutoff, are unchanged.
- Focused verification: AA/configuration tests 26/26; unified estimator tests
  24/24; AutoCombo Vitest 26/26; models.dev sync regression 21/21; core
  typecheck passed; strict OpenSpec validation passed; `git diff --check`
  passed. Independent Luna-xhigh review closed all findings with no residual
  issue. Code Simplifier was applied to the changed calculation code.
- This remains an uncommitted local branch. No push, merge, live setting
  change, or inference was performed. Band membership remains sensitive to
  which benchmark family is removed (7–12 raw IDs in this snapshot); values
  are relative estimates, not success probabilities. Live deployment and
  inference acceptance remain pending.

