  exactly one Phala endpoint with the exact model ID, zero prompt/completion
  pricing, and both `response_format` and `structured_outputs`; otherwise it
  blocks without inference. Successful metadata verification and its check
  time are included in the processor receipt. This metadata check is tested
  with exact, nonzero-price, and multiple-endpoint fixtures.
- Added a one-shot internal chat dispatch for benchmark normalization. It is
  available only through a module-local `WeakMap` marker, requires an active
  OpenRouter API connection whose synced per-connection catalog lists the exact
  model as free, selects the first eligible connection ID in sorted order, and
  pins it. `skipUpstreamRetry` and `emergencyFallbackTried` suppress account
  retry/emergency fallback; the early return also avoids the global 502/503
  fallback. Request includes exact Phala-only provider controls and
  `strict: true` JSON Schema. Output is accepted only when model identity, URL,
  and populated fields are present in an exact returned title/snippet quote.
  Accepted evidence remains candidate-review-required and unrated.
