## Effort-profile scoring design — 2026-10-26

- Owner clarified that effort is a scoring input for band fitness, not a
  capability gate. Keep global `benchmark_fitness` for generic Auto routing;
  add separate low/medium/high rows for band selection.
- Profile mapping: low selects low; medium selects medium; high prefers xhigh
  per model, then high. If exact effort evidence is absent, use unknown-effort
  observations, then that model's median across other efforts as a low-
  confidence proxy. Missing effort is never zero, and reasoning capability
  does not exclude models.
- Keep one median vote per benchmark family, reciprocal coding/general
  fallback, and owner-approved single-family provisional coding scores. Omit
  profile rows with no usable evidence; preserve fallback to existing scores.
- Updated the OpenSpec design, spec delta, tasks, and repo-level TODO with this
  single selected rule. Runtime implementation and tests are still pending;
  do not report profile scores or bands as corrected yet.

